  "_approach": "Hat-doubling shuffle build: bar 1 has only offbeat open hats, bar 2 adds skippy closed 16ths, bar 3 fills the full accented 16th lattice with a shaker, bar 4 pushes open hats to every 8th while a snare 16th roll ramps to 127 and the kick reduces to the downbeat. The heaviest swing in the speed garage set to keep it shuffling. Ref: organ-led '97 shufflers, Attack Magazine's garage-shuffle school. (re-voiced for the Vermona DRM1 MKIII's 8 channels)",
